[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2094322270","pull_request_review_id":2848629834,"id":2094322270,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc581NJe","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"At first I thought delta was an option to consider the parent's TimeScale, but it does not seem to be so. If you want to do this, we may need to add a separate PR to add it to AnimationTree or AnimationMixer. Like:\r\n\r\nanimation_mixer.cpp\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid AnimationMixer::_process_animation(double p_delta, bool p_update_only) {\r\n\t_blend_init();\r\n\tdouble delta = p_delta * Engine::get_singleton()->get_time_scale();\r\n\tif (_blend_pre_process(delta, track_count, track_map)) {\r\n\t\t_blend_capture(delta);\r\n\t\t_blend_calc_total_weight();\r\n\t\t_blend_process(delta, p_update_only);\r\n\t\t_blend_apply();\r\n\t\t_blend_post_process();\r\n\t\temit_signal(SNAME(\"mixer_applied\"));\r\n\t};\r\n\tclear_animation_instances();\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, users should be able to use `AnimMixer.advance(delta * get_time_scale())` or multiply it by duration like `BlendSpace.set_velocity_limit(base * get_time_scale())`.\r\n\r\nConsidering that other Nodes that use time delta do not have those options, it seems to me that we should document the use of Engine.get_time_scale() and leave it to users who really need it.","created_at":"2025-05-18T02:31:35Z","updated_at":"2025-05-18T02:44:29Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2094322270","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2094322270"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2094322270"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2094322270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099154109","pull_request_review_id":2856013126,"id":2099154109,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59Hoy9","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"rdstrcorpse","id":29980512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTgwNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29980512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse","html_url":"https://github.com/rdstrcorpse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"By default the timescale node does affect the blendspace but in my own use case I've found that want to decouple the velocity limiting from the TimeScale node's effect. \r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/7083654f-75a6-4ca8-811c-5c265945d214)\r\nI'll look into another way to do it so that its based the animationtree's advance function/based on the parent's delta as otherwise if we're to use just the default playback delta that will make it impossible for the blendspace to change weights while using velocity limit and timescale is set to 0.0 even if the velocity limit is multiplied to be higher.","created_at":"2025-05-21T02:01:12Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T02:21:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099154109","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099154109"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099154109"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099154109/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099162063","pull_request_review_id":2856034513,"id":2099162063,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59HqvP","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Do you want to bypass the TimeScale and not scale the BlendSpace delta itself, but only change the TimeScale of the child animations?\r\n\r\nI understand the demand for this, but I think it should be a separate PR. I remember we had a discussion somewhere before about having TimeScale as a parameter for all AnimationNodes that have ports.\r\n\r\nSo it should apply to BlendSpace as well as other AnimationNodes at the same time. Then, I suggest just using the default NodeTimeInfo.delta in this PR and adding TimeScale for All AnimationNode in a future PR.","created_at":"2025-05-21T02:11:43Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T02:13:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099162063","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099162063"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099162063"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099162063/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099245620","pull_request_review_id":2856150761,"id":2099245620,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59H_I0","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"rdstrcorpse","id":29980512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTgwNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29980512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse","html_url":"https://github.com/rdstrcorpse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> I understand the demand for this, but I think it should be a separate PR. I remember we had a discussion somewhere before about having TimeScale as a parameter for all AnimationNodes that have ports.\r\n\r\nI did see that in the comments while looking around. It could be just a temporary workaround for now while that hasn't been implemented yet, since 5.0 is quite far away right now. I'd go back and change it in a future pr to fall more in line with the rest when it's in.\r\nOtherwise the blendspace wont be able to change the weights at all while timescale is set 0.0 while without velocity limit it can which doesn't make sense.\r\n\r\nI have made it right now so that its not asking for the engine's delta time but instead the animationtree's which should fall in line more.","created_at":"2025-05-21T03:51:53Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T04:15:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099245620","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099245620"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099245620"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099245620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099419695","pull_request_review_id":2856387366,"id":2099419695,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59Ipov","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The workaround in current is to make every point placed in BlendSpace a nested BlendTree instead of an AnimationNode, and place a TimeScale within the nest for each point, and change all TimeScales simultaneously by script. But I know this is tedious, so which is why we had the discussion like above.","created_at":"2025-05-21T05:57:38Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T05:57:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099419695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099419695"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099419695"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099419695/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099446702","pull_request_review_id":2856428928,"id":2099446702,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59IwOu","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"rdstrcorpse","id":29980512,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI5OTgwNTEy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/29980512?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse","html_url":"https://github.com/rdstrcorpse","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rdstrcorpse/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thats true but for now for the sake of convenience and sanity of anyone trying to use this it would be beneficial to keep it like this (as going through all the blend point's blendtrees in a script would be a nightmare along with editing the blendspace). At a later point when said time scale gets added to the base animation node then it in my opinion it could be made so that the blandspace has 2 timescales 1 that's default and takes care of the child animation nodes and velocity limit and an override time scale that takes care of the velocity limit only if enabled.\r\n\r\nThe default playback still gets used if the override is disabled so nothing is really lost by having this in, its hacky I know that, and it should be (and in a high likelihood will be) replaced asap but its much more beneficial to have this temporarily while the alternative is so tedious at the moment.","created_at":"2025-05-21T06:18:23Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T06:46:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099446702","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099446702"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099446702"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099446702/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099494096","pull_request_review_id":2856505377,"id":2099494096,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOAO6SJc59I7zQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -510,28 +554,56 @@ AnimationNode::NodeTimeInfo AnimationNodeBlendSpace2D::_process(const AnimationM\n \t\t}\n \n \t\tfirst = true;\n-\n \t\tdouble max_weight = 0.0;\n+\n+\t\tint mind_idx = 0;\n+\t\tEngine *eng = Engine::get_singleton();\n+\t\tdouble delta = static_cast<float>(override_delta ? (eng->get_process_step() * eng->get_time_scale()) : pi.delta);","path":"scene/animation/animation_blend_space_2d.cpp","commit_id":"bc39f899188e31a91d75ec7305253683ff161ff0","original_commit_id":"615eb2e5f69f12ab0643ca60125789f9d0b5d181","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No. I disagree with override_delta on consistency and maintainability. When BlendSpace delta is scaled, it should simply multiplys transiton speed, which is consistent with other transition nodes and etc. TimeScale placed on the right just accelerates all time on the left (as well as transition time), and is consistent.\r\n\r\nIf you add a property for a temporary workaround as a band-aid, there will be a breakdown in compatibility when we later deprecate that property by appropreate way such as implement base AnimationNode's TimeScale. So it should not be done, and we will not be able to approve it. Especially since we know the right direction in this case, we should direct our efforts toward making that future PR - In my opinion, it is possible to implement a TimeScale for all AnimationNodes without waiting for 5.0 since there is no compatibility breakdown, but override_delta is bring the compatibility breakdown into there.\r\n\r\nEven without this option, there is certainly a tedious workaround as given above and it should be an effective enough feature for cases that do not use TimeScale.","created_at":"2025-05-21T06:49:45Z","updated_at":"2025-05-21T07:28:11Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099494096","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099494096"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105923#discussion_r2099494096"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105923"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099494096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":561,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2094322270,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":74,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2099631795","pull_request_review_id":2856711544,"id":2099631795,"node_i